* `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 against main, with `code-owner` requested as reviewer. The merge went through with a recorded human approval (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), which satisfies the code-owner requirement.\n\nI didn't re-run CI or check the merged main after the merge. The merge result reports the same commit SHA that passed CI.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the failing test and the money module.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MQSyoT25uSCpkUteohGNhE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GYnYRJ4trosZm6y2x7fuKz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` but its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Checking the test cases: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are both correct under half-even. I'll create the branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XXviz8bBodBoYNj2EDsGYu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UMJxzQAmXmtVBXKpB2J2Mr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money\n\nPer FIN-212, round_money must use banker's rounding. The implementation\nwas using